From: ArchR <noreply@arch-r.io>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtl8xxxu: cancel the works on disconnect

rtl8xxxu_start() submits the RX URBs, schedules ra_watchdog and only
then returns the error of the last URB it could not submit. A dongle
dropping off the bus (an RTL8723BU behind a USB hub on the OTG port,
reconnecting dozens of times) fails that submit with -ENODEV: mac80211
treats the start as failed and never calls stop, so nothing cancels
the watchdog, which re-arms itself every 2 s. rtl8xxxu_disconnect()
then freed the hw with the delayed work still queued: an oops in
ieee80211_iterate_stations_atomic() from rtl8xxxu_watchdog_callback(),
or its timer left in the timer wheel until the block was reused and
__run_timers() panicked on the corrupted entry. Cancel every work in
disconnect, after unregistering, whatever start and stop did.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8xxxu/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8xxxu/core.c
@@ -7999,6 +7999,17 @@
 
 	ieee80211_unregister_hw(hw);
 
+	/*
+	 * rtl8xxxu_start() arms ra_watchdog before it returns the error of
+	 * an RX URB it could not submit (a dongle dropping off the bus), and
+	 * mac80211 calls no stop after a failed start: the watchdog kept
+	 * re-arming and outlived ieee80211_free_hw() below.
+	 */
+	cancel_work_sync(&priv->rx_urb_wq);
+	cancel_work_sync(&priv->c2hcmd_work);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&priv->ra_watchdog);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&priv->update_beacon_work);
+
 	priv->fops->power_off(priv);
 
 	usb_set_intfdata(interface, NULL);
